==English==

===Etymology===
{{rfv-etymology}} Possibly a [[calque]] of Chinese {{etyl|zh}} {{zh-tsp|好久不見|好久不见|[[haojiubujian|hǎojiǔbújiàn]]}} or native American origin.

===Interjection===
{{en-interj|pos=[[long]] [[time]] [[no]] [[see]]}}

# {{idiom}} I haven't seen you for a long time.
#: ''Dave!  '''Long time no see'''!  How has Boston been treating you?''

